    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and the full suite is green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the GOLD membership tier rule: **`membershipTier` becomes `GOLD` when the owner's household (owners sharing the same `householdId`) has 3 or more members after this create; otherwise the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules apply.**\n\nFollowing the codebase's existing pattern (`namesakeCount` is a snapshot value persisted at create time and read back into the mapper-computed tier), I persisted a household-size snapshot rather than recomputing it live \u2014 this matches the spec's \"after this create\" semantics and stays correct across a fresh DB reload.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 sets `owner.setHouseholdMemberCount(countHouseholdMembers(owner))` at create; added `countHouseholdMembers()` = `findHousemates(owner).size() + 1` (existing housemates by same `householdId`, plus the new owner).\n\n2. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added the persisted `householdMemberCount` field (`@Column(name = \"household_member_count\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 the `membershipTier` expression now checks GOLD first (`householdMemberCount >= 3`), falling back to the unchanged SILVER/BRONZE logic.\n\n4. **Schema files** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `household_member_count` column; updated the hsqldb positional seed `INSERT`s (the only positional ones) to include the new column.\n\n5. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 documented the GOLD tier on the `membershipTier` field.\n\nThe `coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold` acceptance test (third household member \u2192 `GOLD`) and the full suite pass: `BUILD SUCCESS`, Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0.\n\nNote: mysql's seed `data.sql` was already inconsistent with its schema before this change (positional inserts with far fewer values than columns) and isn't exercised by the build, so I left it untouched rather than mask a pre-existing issue.",
